  "step_3": "The decision reason requires that the individual prefer the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome, regardless of the monetary difference. In this case, Lottery A has a higher probability (34% vs. 33%), so the reason would prefer A. The individual did note the 1 percentage point difference and the 100 Euro difference, but their justification does not clearly reflect a preference based solely on probability. Instead, the individual appears to be comparing the two aspects (reward and probability) in a trade-off manner, suggesting a more complex evaluation than a simple rule based on probability alone. While the individual did consider the probability difference, the justification does not indicate that the higher probability was the decisive factor. Therefore, it is uncertain whether the decision reason was the primary basis for the choice. The individual may have used the probability difference as part of a broader evaluation, but not as a standalone rule. Thus, the evidence is ambiguous.",
